A||N||11||fiero_se86||t-top or sunroof||||1||
Z||000000||fiero_se86||05-13-2001||12:38 AM||||Hi im 16 and i just bought my first fiero last summer. i want to get it painted this winter but first i wanna put t-tops in or a sunroof, im not sure which one though. i talked to a guy that has t-tops and he said that they leak really bad, and to just get a sunroof. i already know that they will leak b/c my moms camaro has them and they leak. im just wondering which i should go for t-tops or removable sunroof.<BR>thanks <BR>eric||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroHarry||05-13-2001||12:40 AM||||I like my "Vista Veiw" sunroof and think it would be much less hassle for you to have installed......<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA<BR>1985 GT 262K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I>||||reg||12
Z||000002||Coop88||05-13-2001||03:48 AM||||I would go with the sunroof. You can open it while driving, you won't have to cut the frame, and I'll bet they're easier to find (or at least cheaper). ||||reg||10
Z||000003||AusFiero||05-13-2001||11:33 AM||||As a t-top owner I can vouch for the leaks. They are fixable but it just takes time to get it right. And a new set of seals didn't hurt either.<P>From removing them all the time, or more importantly putting them back on I reckon go the sunroof, for cost and convenience.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||05-13-2001||01:00 PM||||My t-tops have never leaked.  I dunno maybe I have just been lucky but the car has been through 210k miles of Northeast U.S. weather (started in NJ, made its way down to Phil., now with me in Baltimore).  The only thing is the replacement parts or lack there of.  If money is not a factor, I would do t-tops personally.  But considering you could install a sunroof for about a 10th of the cost of installing t-tops, I would just settle with a sunroof.||||reg||6
Z||000005||TOM||05-13-2001||03:28 PM||||But dont just put in some hack aftermarket deal. Go with the factory vista vent sunroof. I installed mine in an afternoon.||||reg||1
Z||000006||TheFiero64||05-13-2001||03:39 PM||||I installed the factory sunroof off of my parts car. It has never leaked yet and I have it off on all the nice days.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||perks88gt||05-13-2001||04:57 PM||||Im 24, and i have owned 3 fiero's since I was 15!  I whent through the same thinking you are, I whanted more open air driving, but people told me that t-tops were bad.  Well I didnt listen and I bought a t-top and drove it for 90k miles.  I just recently bought my 3rd fiero, and its a sunroof.  T-top leak, thats a fact.  Anyone who say they dont probably never removed them very frequently.  And that what you should do if you have t-tops.  Secondly, the structual rigidity of the car is greatly compromised to the point that you can notice the chasis flexing.  Just go with the sunroof, there big and offfer about 93% of the same "open air" ability that a t-top does, with no problems.  Trust me i spent 4 years thinking about this!||||reg||13
Z||000008||fiero56||05-13-2001||05:16 PM||||Speaking with t-top owners about the t-top/sunroof debate at shows, most every-one of the t-top owners say the t-tops are very fun when off. But, they have all said also, that the novelty wears off, and they soon finding themselves wishing for a sunroof. Something you can open while driving, etc, etc...||||reg||1
Z||000009||KissMySSFiero||05-13-2001||06:21 PM||||well  my thoughts about this are about the same.  i went thru this too.  i had found some decent ttops at a junk yard for a good price.  i wanted so bad to get them on my car.  however i looked at sunroofs too.  i also want a nice interior inmy car.  if i went with ttops then i would take the risk of ruining my new interior.  and to me its not worth it.  also the novelty would wear off.  and a sunroof is reversable.  ttops you run the risk of not gettin them on right and then your screwed.  worse thing that can happen with a sunroof is you break the a pillar removing it or puting it on.  then  you get another for under $100 bucks at a junk yard.  ttops you have to find.  plus the ttop seals are no longer available and sunroof seals are.  im gettin a sunroof and ill love it either way.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">          <BR>"When in Doubt..Whip it out!!"||||reg||1
Z||000010||RobertVol||05-13-2001||08:38 PM||||Well of course everyone has an opinion. <P>I personally love my T Tops and have them out anytime I get a chance  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>They do not leak at all. I JUST now am needing a new headliner. Not really just sagging A little and I am picky. <P>My car has 61k on it. <P>BUT I may be lucky or fortunate. I will say I hear from most people that they have had problems with their t tops. <P>My suggestions is ...if your on a budget which I think you are. Go with the sunroof. <P>Even if you have small problems with T tops, they're COSTLY to fix! <P>Just my 2 cents!!<P><BR>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1">  <p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 05-13-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000011||fiero_se86||05-13-2001||09:11 PM||||Well everyone i would just like to say thanks for all of your advice. as much as i would like to have t-tops i think ill go for the sunroof. <BR>thanks again<BR>eric||||reg||10
